if (cfs_rq->avg.runnable_sum)
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the CFS parent is not added to the scheduling list when one of its children is unthrottled. This happens when the parent is decayed (i.e., it has no running tasks), leading to a situation where the scheduling hierarchy is inconsistent, resulting in the warning `rq->tmp_alone_branch != &rq->leaf_cfs_rq_list`.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (child_cfs_rq_on_list(cfs_rq))
return false;
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that before determining if a CFS run queue is decayed, it checks if any child CFS run queue is on the list. If a child is present, it indicates that the parent should also be on the list, preventing the parent from being incorrectly marked as decayed and thus maintaining the integrity of the scheduling hierarchy.

